# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SAOS — things that must never be committed
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1. Pre-packaging source delivery.
#    Superseded by artefacts/06-source/, which carries the same code with the
#    --sample flag and redacted sample identity fields. Keep the originals
#    locally as provenance; do not publish them.
SAOS_Source_Library_v0.1/

# 2. Pre-packaging deliverables as originally named.
#    Superseded by artefacts/05-deliverables/, which are renamed to the naming
#    convention. The original workbook filename asserted a provenance its
#    contents did not support — see artefacts/07-reference/QA-FINDINGS.md F-01.
#    Do NOT remove these lines to "fix" a missing file; the correct copies are
#    already committed under artefacts/05-deliverables/.
SAOS Assessment Workbook v0.1.xlsx
SAOS Workbook v0.1 Client 1 retracted Data.xlsx
SAOS Executive Report Template.docx

# 3. Engagement output. Client data is confidential, per-client and
#    retention-managed. It does not belong in version control at any point.
#    Use a path outside the repository entirely.
engagements/
evidence/
Evidence/
*.xlsx.local
SAOS-Assessment-Workbook-v0.1-*-FINAL.*
SAOS-Assessment-Workbook-v0.1-*-DRAFT.*
SAOS-Executive-Report-v0.1-*-FINAL.*
SAOS-Executive-Report-v0.1-*-DRAFT.*

# 4. Node. package.json and package-lock.json ARE committed (reproducible
#    builds); node_modules never is.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.npm/

# 5. Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

